{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.He4ChannelActiveSet","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.He4ChannelActiveSet","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_downstream_uses_only_axioms_not_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_downstream_uses_only_axioms_not_values","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L317-L332","doc":"**Categorical demonstration**: a hypothetical alternative instance\n(with different witness values but the same structural axioms)\nwould discharge all the downstream theorems identically. The\nconjunction below packages the 5 structural axioms without\nreference to specific values.\n\nDefinitionally equal to `he4_class_is_feasible_solution` (since\n`IsHe4LPFeasibleSolution` unfolds to this conjunction). Proof\ndelegates directly to that theorem to avoid duplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_class_is_feasible_solution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_class_is_feasible_solution","kind":"def","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L306-L315","doc":"**Bridge theorem**: any `HasHe4ChannelActiveSet` instance yields\nan `IsHe4LPFeasibleSolution` witness for its tuple. Confirms the\nclass IS a categorical encoding of the abstract feasibility\npredicate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_lp_solution_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_lp_solution_exists","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L287-L304","doc":"**EXISTENCE THEOREM (categorical content of the LP-active-set\nproposition).** There exists a rational LP solution for the ⁴He\nchannel-active-set structure satisfying all 5 categorical axioms.\n\nThis is the pure categorical claim — no specific values; the\nexistential is discharged by the witness-encoded instance.\nDownstream consumers depending only on the EXISTENCE of such a\nsolution (rather than its specific values) can cite this theorem\ndirectly without needing the `[HasHe4ChannelActiveSet]` instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.IsHe4LPFeasibleSolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.IsHe4LPFeasibleSolution","kind":"def","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L263-L285","doc":"**Abstract LP-feasibility predicate** for the ⁴He channel-active-set\nstructure. An 11-tuple `(t_DD, t_Tp, t_He3n, n_target, x_DD, x_Tp,\nx_He3n, y0*, y_DD, y_Tp, y_He3n) ∈ ℚ¹¹` is a feasible LP solution\niff it satisfies all 5 structural axioms (primal saturation, active\nset, dual ordering, cost ordering, strong duality). Categorical:\nno specific values mentioned.\n\nThe witness-encoded instance below provides ONE such solution\n(sourced from the SDP probe), but the predicate accepts any\nrational 11-tuple satisfying the same axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_He3n_active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_He3n_active","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L222-L226","doc":"Channel ³He⊕n is in the LP active set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_Tp_not_active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_Tp_not_active","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L215-L220","doc":"Channel T⊕p is NOT in the LP active set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_DD_active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_DD_active","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L209-L213","doc":"Channel D⊕D is in the LP active set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_DD_costliest_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_DD_costliest_channel","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L203-L207","doc":"D⊕D has strictly the largest channel cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_Tp_cheapest_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_Tp_cheapest_channel","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L194-L201","doc":"T⊕p has the strictly smallest channel cost (smallest binding\nresidual), which is why the LP picks it as the primal-saturating\nchannel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_DD_highest_shadow_price","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_DD_highest_shadow_price","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L185-L192","doc":"D⊕D is the most binding-receptive channel: its dual shadow price\nstrictly exceeds both T⊕p and ³He⊕n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_tp_dual_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_tp_dual_zero","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L179-L183","doc":"T⊕p has zero dual shadow price (complementary-slackness consequence\nof being the primal-saturating channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_dual_ordering_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_dual_ordering_strict","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L171-L177","doc":"D⊕D dual shadow price strictly exceeds ³He⊕n's, which strictly\nexceeds T⊕p's (= 0).  Direct corollary of `dual_ordering`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_primal_obj_eq_tTp_xTp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_primal_obj_eq_tTp_xTp","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L162-L169","doc":"Primal objective collapses to T⊕p contribution because xDD = 0\nand xHe3n = 0 (primal saturation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_strong_duality_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.he4_strong_duality_value","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L155-L160","doc":"Strong duality at the witnessed values: primal_obj = dual_obj. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.instHasHe4ChannelActiveSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.instHasHe4ChannelActiveSet","kind":"instance","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L117-L146","doc":"**Witness-encoded instance** (documentary only).\n\nThe 11 rational fields below are LP-solution approximations from\n`he4-sdp-compositional-probe.witness.json`. Per the audit fix #3,\nthese are NOT class axioms but documentary placeholders satisfying\nthe categorical structural axioms (primal saturation, active set,\ndual ordering, cost ordering, strong duality). Downstream theorems\nconsume only the axioms; any other LP-feasible-and-dual-saturating\n(t, x, y) triple would discharge the class equally well.\n\nThe witness JSON is the authoritative numerical source; this\ninstance exists to make the class type-inhabited for Lean\nelaboration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.strong_duality","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L114-L114","doc":"Strong duality: Σ t_i x_i = n_target · y0_star (LP duality\ngap = 0).  Proved as a rational identity at the witnessed\nvalues; not axiomatised.\n(Needs abstract LP duality infrastructure that does not exist in Mathlib; kept as an honest assumption for models without certificates) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.cost_ordering","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.cost_ordering","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Cost ordering: T⊕p has the smallest channel cost (witness\ninput that motivates the LP picking T⊕p as the primal-\nsaturating channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.dual_ordering","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.dual_ordering","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L105-L105","doc":"Dual ordering: y*_{DD} > y*_{³He⊕n} > y*_{Tp} = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.active_set_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.active_set_eq","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The active set is {D⊕D, ³He⊕n}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.primal_saturating_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.primal_saturating_unique","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The primal-saturating channel is unique and is T⊕p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.yHe3n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.yHe3n","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L99-L99","doc":"Dual shadow price for ³He⊕n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.yTp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.yTp","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L97-L97","doc":"Dual shadow price for T⊕p (must be zero by complementary slackness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.yDD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.yDD","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Dual shadow price for D⊕D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.y0_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.y0_star","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L93-L93","doc":"Dual variable for the binding constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.xHe3n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.xHe3n","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L91-L91","doc":"Primal weight on ³He⊕n channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.xTp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.xTp","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Primal weight on T⊕p channel (the saturating one). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.xDD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.xDD","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L87-L87","doc":"Primal weight on D⊕D channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.n_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.n_target","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Binding target: Δ_coupling(2,2) ≈ 13.197 MeV. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.tHe3n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.tHe3n","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Cost coefficient for ³He⊕n (channel binding residual). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.tTp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.tTp","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Cost coefficient for T⊕p (channel binding residual). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.tDD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.tDD","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Cost coefficient for D⊕D (channel binding residual). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.HasHe4ChannelActiveSet","kind":"class","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L54-L115","doc":"Class encoding the LP-solution **structural axioms** for ⁴He.\n\n**Audit fix #3 (PR followup, 2026-05-25):** the class fields\n(`tDD`, `tTp`, ... `yHe3n`) carry rational LP-solution data\nsourced from `he4-sdp-compositional-probe.witness.json` — but\nthe **categorical content** consumed by downstream theorems is\npurely the AXIOMS:\n  - `primal_saturating_unique` (xTp uniquely positive)\n  - `active_set_eq` ({DD, ³He+n}, not Tp)\n  - `dual_ordering` (yDD > yHe3n > yTp = 0)\n  - `cost_ordering` (tTp < tHe3n < tDD)\n  - `strong_duality` (gap = 0)\n\nNone of the downstream theorems (he4_strong_duality_value,\nhe4_primal_obj_eq_tTp_xTp, he4_DD_highest_shadow_price, ...)\ndepend on the specific witness values — only on the STRUCTURAL\naxioms. The class IS categorical; the instance below is one\nwitness, the witness JSON is the authoritative source.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond, this class is the sole `sorry`-equivalent\ninput for downstream propositions; the empirical numerics are\nLIVE in the witness JSON, with the class providing the structural\ninterface. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:he4-channel-active-set","label":"prop:he4-channel-active-set","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel.InActiveSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel.InActiveSet","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L44-L50","doc":"A channel is in the active set iff its dual shadow price is\nstrictly positive (constraint is tight on the LP dual side). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.instReprChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.instReprChannel","kind":"instance","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.instReprChannel.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.instReprChannel.repr","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.instDecidableEqChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.instDecidableEqChannel","kind":"instance","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel.He3n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel.He3n","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel.Tp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel.Tp","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel.DD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel.DD","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4ChannelActiveSet.Channel","kind":"inductive","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-channel-active-set.lean#L35-L40","doc":"Discrete index of the three primary ⁴He compositional channels. ","signatureChunk":0}]}